# XSH strxfrm() and strxfrm_l()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Run in the POSIX locale. Only values the text defines are checked: the length
# returned, the relation between strcmp() of the results and strcoll() of the
# originals, and that no more than n bytes are written. Destinations are filled
# with 'X' first so that bytes written past n show. When the value returned is n
# or more, the contents are unspecified and are not looked at. The locale-object
# tests use newlocale() for "C" (failure to make one is UNRESOLVED); the one with
# another global locale needs pc_find_locale("UTF-8", 0), NOTINUSE without. The
# may-fail EINVAL is not provoked.

assertion  XSH.strxfrm.001
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With room for the whole result, strxfrm() of "abc" returns a
           length equal to the strlen() of the string it stored (a NUL ends
           the result at that index).
test       t/001-length.c

assertion  XSH.strxfrm.002
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       For every pair taken from twelve strings of portable characters,
           the sign of strcmp() on the two transformed strings equals the
           sign of strcoll() on the originals.
test       t/002-order.c

assertion  XSH.strxfrm.003
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With n 3 on "abcdef", no byte at index 3 or later is written, and
           the value returned equals the one returned when there is room for
           everything.
test       t/003-n-bound.c

assertion  XSH.strxfrm.004
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With n 0 the destination may be a null pointer: the call returns
           the same length as the call with room for everything.
test       t/004-n-zero.c

assertion  XSH.strxfrm.005
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       strxfrm_l() with a locale object for "C": the length returned is the
           strlen() of the stored string, n 0 with a null destination gives the
           same length, and for pairs of strings the sign of strcmp() on the
           transformed strings equals that of strcoll_l() on the originals.
test       t/005-locale-object.c

assertion  XSH.strxfrm.006
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       strxfrm() and strxfrm_l() leave errno unchanged when they succeed,
           both when it is 0 and when it is EDOM.
test       t/006-errno-kept.c

assertion  XSH.strxfrm.007
anchor     functions/strxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       strxfrm_l() uses its object, not the global locale: with another locale
           as the global locale, results of an object for "C" compare with
           strcmp() as the strcoll_l() results of that object do, for pairs that
           include "B" and "a" (which collate "B" first in the POSIX locale).
test       t/007-object-independent.c
